1
00:00:02,230 --> 00:00:07,199
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, Madinan Period, Volume 2

2
00:00:07,779 --> 00:00:09,681
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki;

3
00:00:10,784 --> 00:00:13,810
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:13,973 --> 00:00:16,565
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد

5
00:00:16,755 --> 00:00:19,446
وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

6
00:00:20,255 --> 00:00:22,081
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمةُ الله وَبَرَكَاتُه’

7
00:00:22,982 --> 00:00:26,072
Rasool Allah ﷺ had a dream,

8
00:00:26,704 --> 00:00:34,226
he saw that he was making Tawaf(طواف) around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) along with the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

9
00:00:34,718 --> 00:00:39,699
and then they shaved their heads and some of them shorten their hair after that.

10
00:00:40,716 --> 00:00:52,332
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ now, it has been six years since he has left Makkah along with the Muhajireen رضي الله عنهم

11
00:00:52,967 --> 00:00:56,251
and they dearly missed, Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

12
00:00:56,795 --> 00:01:03,808
Makkah the greatest of the land of Allahعَزّوجَلّ it was beloved to them

13
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:09,711
 because of the religious reasons and also because it was their home.

14
00:01:10,256 --> 00:01:14,917
So, they were longing to go back to Makkah and visit Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

15
00:01:15,352 --> 00:01:19,268
and as one of Mufassireen(مفسرين) said: Commenting on the Ayah(آية).

16
00:01:19,601 --> 00:01:22,003
وَإِذْ جَعَلْنَا الْبَيْتَ مَثَابَةً لِلنَّاسِ

17
00:01:22,484 --> 00:01:25,157
We have made the house of Allah Masabah(مَثَابَةْ)

18
00:01:25,474 --> 00:01:30,564
Masabah(مَثَابَةْ) means a place that you want to return to, all the time.

19
00:01:30,933 --> 00:01:33,018
And this Mufassir(مفسر) gave the example

20
00:01:33,553 --> 00:01:40,495
he said, that the young camel whenever, it would go away, to play

21
00:01:40,795 --> 00:01:44,091
it would always want to come back to its mother

22
00:01:44,771 --> 00:01:49,384
just to see the mother and touch the mother and then it would go and play again,

23
00:01:49,409 --> 00:01:52,724
just to feel the comfort that the mother is still there.

24
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:58,414
And he gave this analogy to the believer and Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

25
00:01:58,590 --> 00:02:03,074
The believer whenever he see's Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) the first time

26
00:02:03,124 --> 00:02:06,197
 whenever, he goes around at the first time, he's hooked for life.

27
00:02:07,112 --> 00:02:11,247
And he would always want to return back again and again to visit it

28
00:02:11,598 --> 00:02:15,696
and even though he might be a foreigner in Makkah but he feels at home.

29
00:02:16,107 --> 00:02:19,569
 Even though, it's not his home he might not speak the language

30
00:02:19,625 --> 00:02:23,180
 but he feels at home, as soon as he enters into Al-Haram(اَلْحَرم).

31
00:02:23,514 --> 00:02:30,998
And Rasool Allah ﷺ has called on, invited the Muslims of Madina

32
00:02:31,038 --> 00:02:36,571
 and the surrounding areas the tribes that have become Muslim around Al-Madina(اَلْمدينة),

33
00:02:36,611 --> 00:02:40,024
 he invited them all to come out with him for Umrah(عمرة)

34
00:02:40,356 --> 00:02:47,348
and the ones who responded to his call numbered around fourteen hundred, a sizable number

35
00:02:47,801 --> 00:02:52,834
and they set out on the path towards Makkah.

36
00:02:53,174 --> 00:02:55,388
When they reach to Dhul-Khaleefah(ذوالخليفه),

37
00:02:55,452 --> 00:03:01,372
which is the Meeqaat(ميقات) of Ahlul-Madina(اهل المدينه) that's a place where they start their Ehraam(إحرام).

38
00:03:01,716 --> 00:03:07,271
Rasool Allah ﷺ he told the Muslims to put on their garments of Ehraam(إحرام)

39
00:03:07,425 --> 00:03:10,460
and to mark the sacrificial animals,

40
00:03:10,553 --> 00:03:17,436
which was the tradition that the animals that are set for sacrifice are marked

41
00:03:17,975 --> 00:03:21,130
 and Rasool Allah ﷺ had with him 70 camels

42
00:03:21,558 --> 00:03:23,093
and they started making Talbih(تلبيح)

43
00:03:23,133 --> 00:03:24,437
 لَبَّيْكْ اَلَّلهُمَّ لَبَّيْكْ

44
00:03:24,859 --> 00:03:26,451
The procession was peaceful.

45
00:03:26,718 --> 00:03:29,265
Rasool Allah ﷺ intended, no fighting

46
00:03:29,559 --> 00:03:32,919
and therefore he did not take with him any arms

47
00:03:33,189 --> 00:03:41,664
except for the swords in their sheaths and an Arab man would never travel without his sword

48
00:03:42,482 --> 00:03:45,548
but this was not an army set out to fight,

49
00:03:45,810 --> 00:03:50,435
this was an army going out for the Ibadah(عبادة), the ritual of Umrah(عمرة).

50
00:03:51,474 --> 00:03:55,737
However, Rasool Allah ﷺ even though this was his intention

51
00:03:55,761 --> 00:04:01,233
but Rasool Allah ﷺ was very careful, very alert and he would not be taken by surprise

52
00:04:01,566 --> 00:04:08,464
 and therefore, he had 20 men on horse, horseback ahead of him

53
00:04:09,028 --> 00:04:12,507
 as a protection and also to clear the route

54
00:04:12,975 --> 00:04:15,635
and check, if there's any dangers on the way.

55
00:04:15,962 --> 00:04:21,140
And he also sent a spy for reconnaissance to gather information for him

56
00:04:21,463 --> 00:04:27,480
and the man responsible for this mission was Bishar Ibn Sufiyan(بشرإبن سفيان),

57
00:04:27,683 --> 00:04:33,110
while the man who was appointed over the horsemen was Abbad Bin Bishr رضي الله عنه.

58
00:04:33,873 --> 00:04:38,645
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was a very alert man, very careful,

59
00:04:39,152 --> 00:04:43,020
he was a man known to attend to the details

60
00:04:43,737 --> 00:04:45,638
and as he said about himself.

61
00:04:45,678 --> 00:04:47,718
 لَسْتُ بِالْخِبِّ وَلا الخِب يَخْدَعْنِيْ

62
00:04:48,029 --> 00:04:52,568
I am not a trickster, but the trickster cannot trick me.

63
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:58,419
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه could not be taken by surprise and could not be tricked

64
00:04:58,836 --> 00:05:00,221
and everybody knew that about him

65
00:05:00,544 --> 00:05:05,591
and that's reflected through his words, and statements, and the advice, that he would give Rasool Allah ﷺ

66
00:05:05,636 --> 00:05:09,506
 as we can see throughout the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

67
00:05:09,725 --> 00:05:11,136
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) told him;

68
00:05:11,437 --> 00:05:16,160
 يا رسول الله تَدْخُلُ عَلى قَوْمٍ هُمْ لَكَ الْحَرْبْ بِغَيْرِ سلاح و لا قراع

69
00:05:16,395 --> 00:05:21,943
O Messenger of Allah, are you going to enter on a people, who are in the state of war with you, without any weapons?

70
00:05:22,297 --> 00:05:27,682
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ agreed with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and he called the weapons from Madina

71
00:05:27,706 --> 00:05:34,502
 but they were to be separate from the group, which Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه), it would be separate.

72
00:05:34,571 --> 00:05:36,264
They would have their weapon separate because

73
00:05:36,450 --> 00:05:40,312
they wanted everybody to see that they have came for peaceful mission, tayyeb(طيب).

74
00:05:40,337 --> 00:05:49,513
Now, the man sent on reconnaissance he came back, this man Bishr Bin Sufiaan(بِشربن سفيان), he came back to Rasool Allah ﷺ

75
00:05:50,090 --> 00:05:54,877
and told him that Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) has actually marched out and they're preparing for war.

76
00:05:55,584 --> 00:05:57,089
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

77
00:05:57,129 --> 00:05:59,898
اَشِيْرُوْا عَلَيَّ اَيُّهَاالنَّاسْ اَتَرَوْنَا

78
00:06:00,249 --> 00:06:05,745
اَنْ اَمِيْلَ اِلَى عِيَالِهِمْ وَذراري هؤلاء الَّذِيْنَ يُرِيْدُوْنَ اِنْ يَّصُدُّوْنَا عَنِّ الْبَيْتْ

79
00:06:06,278 --> 00:06:07,821
Men give me your advice,

80
00:06:08,217 --> 00:06:15,949
Do you think that I should head for the children and families of those, who wished to keep us from Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).?

81
00:06:16,976 --> 00:06:18,479
You see, brothers and sisters

82
00:06:19,479 --> 00:06:26,044
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) held a very high status in Arabia among the Arab tribes.

83
00:06:26,501 --> 00:06:29,109
That is because they were custodians of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

84
00:06:29,653 --> 00:06:34,797
but it was a known tradition, it was known common knowledge among the people

85
00:06:35,161 --> 00:06:41,416
that no one should prevent, anyone from Hajj(حَجْ) and Umrah(عمرة).

86
00:06:42,554 --> 00:06:48,591
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are now trying to prevent Muhammadﷺ and the Muslims from entering Makkah

87
00:06:48,704 --> 00:06:52,323
and this is unheard of, it is something that you don't do.

88
00:06:52,568 --> 00:06:55,334
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is asking the companions

89
00:06:55,911 --> 00:06:59,973
should we head for the children and families of those,

90
00:07:00,426 --> 00:07:01,459
who are those?

91
00:07:01,881 --> 00:07:09,767
Rasool Allah ﷺ is here talking about the tribes, who allied themselves with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

92
00:07:10,321 --> 00:07:14,939
in this horrible mission of preventing the Muslims from entering into Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

93
00:07:15,118 --> 00:07:18,855
because Bishr(بشر), when it came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, he said;

94
00:07:19,062 --> 00:07:24,076
اِنَّ قُرَيْشً قَدْ جَمْعُوْ لَكَ جَمْعًا وَجَمْعُوْ لَكَ الْاَحَابِيْشْ

95
00:07:24,341 --> 00:07:30,796
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) have mobilized themselves, and they have also mobilized Al-Ahabeish(ألأحابيش),

96
00:07:30,820 --> 00:07:33,932
Al-Ahabeish(ألأحابيش) is the confederation of tribes

97
00:07:34,279 --> 00:07:38,762
three or more tribes that have allied themselves with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

98
00:07:39,551 --> 00:07:42,403
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying;

99
00:07:42,633 --> 00:07:49,123
How about we attack the families and children of these other tribes?

100
00:07:50,312 --> 00:07:56,598
So, that they would have to come back and protect their families

101
00:07:56,820 --> 00:08:00,299
 while then we could move on towards Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

102
00:08:00,324 --> 00:08:02,826
تَكُوْنُ عُنُقًا قَدْ قَطَاحَ الله

103
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:08,542
So, by this we would break the alliance and split up their army

104
00:08:08,796 --> 00:08:14,855
Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه he answered, he gave his opinion, he said;

105
00:08:15,344 --> 00:08:18,917
يا رسول الله خَرَجْتَ عَامِدً لِّهَذَالْبَيْتْ

106
00:08:19,326 --> 00:08:26,010
لَا تريد قَتْلَ اَحَدٍ وَلَا حَرْبَ اَحَدْ فَتَوَجَّه لَهْ فَمَنْ صدَّنَا عنه قَاتَلْنَاه

107
00:08:26,334 --> 00:08:30,607
Messenger of Allah, you have come forth to visit Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

108
00:08:30,766 --> 00:08:34,741
not intending to do battle or to make war against anyone.

109
00:08:35,115 --> 00:08:39,372
Proceed to it, and we will fight anybody who blocks our way.

110
00:08:39,396 --> 00:08:45,031
This was the opinion Abu-Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه and Rasool Allah ﷺ agreed with him

111
00:08:45,071 --> 00:08:52,252
 and therefore the plans of attacking these Kuffar(كفار) in their residence were stopped.

112
00:08:52,699 --> 00:08:53,648
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

113
00:08:53,688 --> 00:08:55,323
اُمضُوْا عَلَى بَرَكَة الله

114
00:08:55,396 --> 00:08:58,000
then proceed onwards in Allah's name.

115
00:08:59,159 --> 00:09:08,474
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) have sent a force of 200 men led by Khalid Ibn Waleed رضي الله عنه and Ikrimah Bin Abi Jahel(عِكرِمَة بن ابي جهل).

116
00:09:09,127 --> 00:09:15,094
When Rasool Allah ﷺ received that piece of information he announced to his army and said;

117
00:09:15,189 --> 00:09:20,545
 Who will take us on a path that will take us around them

118
00:09:20,866 --> 00:09:27,920
so a man from Aslam(أسلم), he offered to guide them through a back road

119
00:09:28,316 --> 00:09:32,472
so to speak, it was very rough difficult terrain

120
00:09:33,077 --> 00:09:37,588
but eventually they made it, to the plain of Al-Hudaybiyya(ألْحُدَيْبِيَةْ)

121
00:09:37,867 --> 00:09:42,623
which is to the south of Makkah and it was only a days walk from the holy city.

122
00:09:42,776 --> 00:09:49,081
When Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) received this information that the Muslims have went around him

123
00:09:49,639 --> 00:09:52,280
and then he rushed back, towards Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

124
00:09:52,565 --> 00:09:57,664
and now Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) knew that Rasool Allah ﷺ is only days distance from them.

125
00:09:58,824 --> 00:10:01,109
When Rasool Allah ﷺ reached to Al-Hudaybiyya(ألْحُدَيْبِيَةْ)

126
00:10:01,535 --> 00:10:05,028
his camel Al-Qaswaa(اَلْقَصْوَاء), the famous camel of Rasool Allah ﷺ

127
00:10:05,052 --> 00:10:08,157
which we have talked about in our earlier session.

128
00:10:08,758 --> 00:10:12,976
Al-Qaswaa(اَلْقَصْوَاء) sat down, and when they would tell her; Hal(هل), Hal(هل)

129
00:10:13,016 --> 00:10:20,286
which is the word that they would use to ask the camel to stand up and move the camel refused,

130
00:10:20,818 --> 00:10:23,951
the camel refused to stand up.

131
00:10:24,502 --> 00:10:25,191
So, they said;

132
00:10:25,231 --> 00:10:26,654
خَلَاَتِ الْقَصْوَاء

133
00:10:26,922 --> 00:10:28,892
Al-Qaswaa(اَلْقَصْوَاء) has become refractory.

134
00:10:28,990 --> 00:10:36,140
With these animals, camels, horses donkeys, the animals that are used for transportation,

135
00:10:36,393 --> 00:10:41,702
sometimes they become obstinate and they suddenly refuse to take orders.

136
00:10:42,239 --> 00:10:43,932
So, the people  were saying;

137
00:10:43,972 --> 00:10:44,956
 خَلَتِ الْقَصْوَاء

138
00:10:44,996 --> 00:10:46,892
 it has become refractory.

139
00:10:47,196 --> 00:10:48,606
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

140
00:10:48,813 --> 00:10:52,106
 وَمَا خَلَتِ الْقَصْوَاءْ وَمَا هُوَ (ذَاكَ)لَهَا بِخُلُقْ

141
00:10:52,367 --> 00:10:56,410
Al-Qaswaa(اَلْقَصْوَاء) has not, and that is not in her nature.

142
00:10:57,063 --> 00:11:00,091
وَلَكِنْ حَبَسَهَا حَابِسُ الْفِيْلْ

143
00:11:00,392 --> 00:11:04,233
But she has been held back by Him, Who held back to the elephant.

144
00:11:04,386 --> 00:11:06,913
You remember the story of the elephant,

145
00:11:07,262 --> 00:11:13,558
Abraha(اَبْرَاهَةْ), and his army when they were attacking Makkah, the elephant refused to proceed.

146
00:11:13,734 --> 00:11:17,681
But when they would turn the elephant around, it would suddenly run away,

147
00:11:18,076 --> 00:11:21,406
they would turn it back to Makkah, and it would refuse to move.

148
00:11:21,638 --> 00:11:23,111
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

149
00:11:23,318 --> 00:11:29,533
The One, Who has held back the elephant is the One, Who held back the camel.

150
00:11:29,892 --> 00:11:34,544
But there's a big difference here, then it was Abraha(اَبْرَاهَةْ) and the kuffar(كفار)

151
00:11:34,711 --> 00:11:37,851
and now, it is Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه).

152
00:11:38,115 --> 00:11:40,293
So, what does this mean?

153
00:11:40,317 --> 00:11:43,082
Ibn Hajar(اِبْن حجَر) comments on this and says;

154
00:11:43,609 --> 00:11:49,078
Allahعَزّوجَلّ knew then and now that the people of Makkah are going to become Muslim

155
00:11:49,386 --> 00:11:53,259
and therefore, he prevented bloodshed then, and now.

156
00:11:53,622 --> 00:11:57,852
Then, it was by destroying the army of Abraha(اَبْرَاهَةْ) and his followers

157
00:11:58,333 --> 00:12:02,447
and now, it is by opening up the doors to peace

158
00:12:02,905 --> 00:12:07,106
and if Rasool Allah ﷺ had proceeded onward

159
00:12:07,290 --> 00:12:09,235
and war would had ensued,

160
00:12:09,449 --> 00:12:11,024
 there would have been a lot of bloodshed.

161
00:12:11,338 --> 00:12:15,237
But Allahسبحانه وتعالى, held back the Muslims and they stopped

162
00:12:15,356 --> 00:12:19,571
 when Al-Qaswaa(اَلْقَصْوَاء) has refused to move.

163
00:12:19,714 --> 00:12:26,911
Eventually, it did move, but this event, Rasool Allah ﷺ turned our attention to it,

164
00:12:27,065 --> 00:12:30,908
that it is something done by Allahعَزّوجَلّ

165
00:12:31,170 --> 00:12:35,884
and this was the explanation given by Ibn Hajar رَحِمَهُ الله.

166
00:12:36,678 --> 00:12:41,890
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: By Him, Who holds my soul in His hand,

167
00:12:42,285 --> 00:12:46,194
I'll accept any request that, they make of me

168
00:12:46,433 --> 00:12:49,559
by which the sanctuaries of Allah are dignified

169
00:12:49,774 --> 00:12:51,102
and in another narration,

170
00:12:51,268 --> 00:12:55,141
in which the ties of family are honored.

171
00:12:56,213 --> 00:12:59,147
Rasool Allah ﷺ had announced and made it clear

172
00:12:59,179 --> 00:13:03,118
that he intends on peace and he will accept any offer that they make

173
00:13:03,497 --> 00:13:06,738
as long as the commands of Allah are  honored.

174
00:13:08,086 --> 00:13:09,491
There was a well in Hudaybiyya(حُدَيْبِيَّةْ)

175
00:13:09,515 --> 00:13:12,061
but when the Sahabah(صحابه) went to drink from the well, it was empty.

176
00:13:12,490 --> 00:13:14,840
So, they came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, to tell him about it

177
00:13:14,865 --> 00:13:18,469
Rasool Allah ﷺ, he gave him an arrow from his quiver

178
00:13:18,493 --> 00:13:23,278
and told them to take it, and drop it into the well and they did so.

179
00:13:23,392 --> 00:13:28,320
 And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) water started coming out from this well.

180
00:13:28,725 --> 00:13:35,764
There are many miracles of similar sort, that happened to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

181
00:13:36,851 --> 00:13:38,734
Skirmishes would happen

182
00:13:39,262 --> 00:13:46,127
and prisoners were taken by Rasool Allah ﷺ from the Mushrikeen(مشركين) but no one was killed.

183
00:13:46,151 --> 00:13:50,647
One example was narrated by Salamah Ibn Aqwa رضي الله عنه

184
00:13:51,041 --> 00:13:52,509
He said: I was sleeping under a tree

185
00:13:52,549 --> 00:13:58,065
and there were some Mushrikeen(مشركين) lying down under an adjacent tree.

186
00:13:58,432 --> 00:14:00,930
And they were speaking against Rasool Allah ﷺ

187
00:14:00,954 --> 00:14:06,350
so I went to sleep under a tree, in the distance.

188
00:14:06,546 --> 00:14:10,104
I didn't want to hear the rubbish that, they were talking about.

189
00:14:10,544 --> 00:14:15,020
Then I heard the call to arms something has happened.

190
00:14:15,060 --> 00:14:18,737
 So, there was a call of Al-Muhajireen(ألمهاجرين)

191
00:14:19,397 --> 00:14:24,770
and Salamah(سلمه) said: So, I rushed towards these four Mushrikeen(مشركين), who were sleeping under this tree

192
00:14:25,034 --> 00:14:28,427
and they had their swords hanging on the branches of this tree.

193
00:14:28,595 --> 00:14:32,952
So, I gathered all of their swords and had them, under my arm

194
00:14:33,167 --> 00:14:39,683
and I had my sword in my arm and I told them if any one of you makes any move I'm gonna chop off his head

195
00:14:40,130 --> 00:14:43,632
and I took them as prisoners to Rasool Allah ﷺ, four of them.

196
00:14:45,003 --> 00:14:47,469
So, there were events of this sort.

197
00:14:47,668 --> 00:14:50,574
The situation was very delicate

198
00:14:51,062 --> 00:14:55,165
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to send an envoy into Makkah,

199
00:14:55,252 --> 00:14:58,530
 to explain to them that we have not come with the intention of fighting,

200
00:14:58,570 --> 00:15:02,221
we have come to make Tawaf(طواف) around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

201
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:05,409
Rasool Allah ﷺ chose Kharaash Ibn Umayyah(خراش بن إمية)

202
00:15:05,686 --> 00:15:08,274
who's from the tribe of Khuza'a(خزاعة),

203
00:15:08,747 --> 00:15:12,167
Kharash(خراش) went into Makkah, how did they deal with him?

204
00:15:12,334 --> 00:15:15,403
They kill his camel and they almost killed him

205
00:15:15,711 --> 00:15:19,547
until, the Ahabeesh(أحابيش) interfered and protected him.

206
00:15:19,572 --> 00:15:22,647
So, this is how they dealt with the envoy of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

207
00:15:22,749 --> 00:15:27,433
You can see throughout the story that Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were in a state of despair

208
00:15:27,667 --> 00:15:31,310
they were confused, they were desperate, and they were frustrated.

209
00:15:31,728 --> 00:15:35,522
They were people who are arrogant and now they were humiliated.

210
00:15:35,839 --> 00:15:38,108
They were losing their position in Arabia

211
00:15:38,417 --> 00:15:42,352
and their pride was preventing them from seeing clearly.

212
00:15:42,377 --> 00:15:46,927
So, you see a lot of frustration in the way they were behaving

213
00:15:47,221 --> 00:15:49,571
Kharaash Ibn Umayyah(خراش بن إمية) is coming to announce to them

214
00:15:49,595 --> 00:15:52,341
first of all he's a messenger and messengers are not killed

215
00:15:52,892 --> 00:15:58,170
and second of all, he's coming to tell them that we have not come for the purpose of fighting

216
00:15:58,318 --> 00:16:00,550
and this is how they dealt with him, so he left.

217
00:16:00,812 --> 00:16:03,217
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to send someone else

218
00:16:03,471 --> 00:16:07,012
so he summoned Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه

219
00:16:07,711 --> 00:16:10,098
and he told him, his intentions.

220
00:16:10,201 --> 00:16:13,629
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) he responded back and said;

221
00:16:13,997 --> 00:16:17,851
There is none of my family Bannu Udae(بنوعدي)

222
00:16:18,159 --> 00:16:22,774
who's left in Makkah to give me a protection, and Quraish(قريش);

223
00:16:23,059 --> 00:16:25,343
 وَقَدْ عَلِمَتْ قُرَيْش عَدَاوَتِي لَهَا

224
00:16:25,367 --> 00:16:29,159
And Quraish(قريش) they know very well, my animosity towards them.

225
00:16:29,866 --> 00:16:33,330
But if you insist on me going, then I will go.

226
00:16:34,553 --> 00:16:38,168
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) gave a frank assessment of the situation

227
00:16:38,415 --> 00:16:41,964
that he believes that he would be in danger, if he goes into Makkah

228
00:16:42,117 --> 00:16:44,056
but if it's an order then he will obey.

229
00:16:44,366 --> 00:16:48,319
Rasool Allah ﷺ was silent, so then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) suggested another name.

230
00:16:48,456 --> 00:16:54,368
He said: But how about you send Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) because his clan are there.

231
00:16:54,587 --> 00:16:57,396
Now, Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) belongs to Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّه)

232
00:16:57,658 --> 00:17:02,171
and Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّه) are from the major branch of Quraish(قريش)

233
00:17:02,676 --> 00:17:06,225
Bannu Abd-Manaf(بنوعبدالمناف) there were two families in Quraish(قريش)

234
00:17:06,612 --> 00:17:11,535
that held the reins of leadership in the town

235
00:17:11,859 --> 00:17:14,955
and these were Bannu Makhzoom(بنومخذوم) and Bannu Abd-Manaf(بنوعبدالمناف)

236
00:17:15,311 --> 00:17:21,002
Bannu Makhzoom(بنومخذوم) among the famous personalities of Bannu Makhzoom(بنومخذوم) are;

237
00:17:21,042 --> 00:17:26,464
 Abu Jahal(ابوجهل), who was the head of Quraish(قريش) until, his death.

238
00:17:26,886 --> 00:17:30,241
And he was the leader in the fight against the Muslims.

239
00:17:30,643 --> 00:17:34,412
And then you have Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(إلوليد إبن مغيرة) and Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) his son,

240
00:17:34,768 --> 00:17:37,144
these belong to the clan of Bannu Makhzoom(بنومخذوم).

241
00:17:37,288 --> 00:17:38,688
And then you have Bannu Abd-Manaf(بنوعبدالمناف)

242
00:17:38,728 --> 00:17:41,450
and the two major branches of Bannu Abd-Manaf(بنوعبدالمناف) are;

243
00:17:41,490 --> 00:17:44,860
Bannu Hashim(بنوهاشم), the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ and Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّه).

244
00:17:44,884 --> 00:17:49,865
So Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّه), by the way are very close relatives of Bannu Hashim(بنوهاشم).

245
00:17:50,213 --> 00:17:52,899
Now, Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) belong to Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّه).

246
00:17:53,763 --> 00:17:56,913
So, when Rasool Allah ﷺ sent him to Makkah,

247
00:17:57,542 --> 00:18:05,660
he was immediately, given protection by the major figure of Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّه) after Abu Sufiyan(ابوسُفيان),

248
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:08,643
see Abu Sufiyan(ابوسُفيان) also belongs to Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّه) but he wasn't there at the time.

249
00:18:08,739 --> 00:18:14,539
So, the one who gave protection to Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) was his cousin Abbaan Bin Saeed Bin Al-Aas(عَبَّان بن سَعِيد بن اَلْعَاص).

250
00:18:14,878 --> 00:18:19,940
He had him ride with him on his camel and he went in front of Quraish(قريش) and said;

251
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:22,150
This man is under my protection.

252
00:18:22,482 --> 00:18:25,025
Who would dare now to touch Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان),

253
00:18:25,395 --> 00:18:29,606
when he entered in the protection of Abbaan Bin Saeed Bin Al-Aas(عَبَّان بن سَعِيد بن اَلْعَاص).

254
00:18:30,112 --> 00:18:32,999
The mission of Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) was two fold.

255
00:18:33,761 --> 00:18:39,803
Number one: He would announce to Quraish(قريش) that the Muslims have not come for war.

256
00:18:40,049 --> 00:18:47,143
Number two: He was told by Rasool Allah ﷺ to visit the believing men and believing women

257
00:18:47,421 --> 00:18:52,673
and give them the glad tidings that Islam will be victorious that the Muslims will win.

258
00:18:53,316 --> 00:18:57,174
Uthman Ibn Affan رضي الله عنه he went to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and told them.

259
00:18:57,421 --> 00:19:01,812
بَعَثَنِيْ رَسُولِ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم لِيَدْعُوْكُمْ اِلَى الاِسْلَامْ

260
00:19:02,082 --> 00:19:06,400
وَاِلَى اللهِ جَلَّ ثَنَاءُ وَتَدْخُلُوْنَ فِيْ الدِّيْنِ كَآفَّهْ

261
00:19:06,685 --> 00:19:10,907
فَاِنَّ الله مُظْهِرُ دِيْنِهِ وَ مُعِزْ نَبِيِّهِ

262
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:17,351
Rasool Allah ﷺ sent me to you to call you to Islam and to Allah

263
00:19:17,515 --> 00:19:20,496
and that you enter in the religion of Allah

264
00:19:20,858 --> 00:19:26,936
because Allah will give victory to His religion and will honor His Prophet.

265
00:19:27,104 --> 00:19:33,167
وَاُخْرَى تُكْفَوْنَ وَيَكُوْنُ الَّذِيْ يَلِّيْ هَذَالْاَمْرْ مِنْه غَيْرُكُمْ

266
00:19:33,578 --> 00:19:37,624
فَاِنْ ظفِرَ بِرَسُوْلَ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وَسلم فَذَالِكَ مَا اَرَدْتُّمْ

267
00:19:37,706 --> 00:19:40,402
وَاِنْ ظفَرَ كُنْتُمْ بِالخِيَّارْ

268
00:19:40,581 --> 00:19:43,478
بَيْنَ اَنْ تَدْخُلُوْ فِيْمَا دَخَلَ فِيهِالنَّاسْ

269
00:19:43,502 --> 00:19:47,098
اَوْ تُقَاتِلُوْ وَاَنْتُمْ وَافِرُوْنَ جَامُوْنْ

270
00:19:47,270 --> 00:19:51,121
اِنَّ الْحَرْبَ قَدْ نَهِكَتْكُمْ وَاَذْهَبَتِ الْاَمَاثِلَ مِنْكُمْ

271
00:19:51,821 --> 00:19:57,159
And then he told them: And let someone else take care of this affair.

272
00:19:57,827 --> 00:20:04,105
So, if they defeat the Messenger of Allah, then that is what you are asking for

273
00:20:04,367 --> 00:20:11,965
 and if he wins then you have the option of either following what the rest of the people have followed

274
00:20:12,125 --> 00:20:15,343
or you fight and you have taken some rest

275
00:20:15,449 --> 00:20:21,102
because war has exhausted you, and the best among you have been killed.

276
00:20:22,191 --> 00:20:26,056
Very direct and blunt message telling them that you're exhausted,

277
00:20:26,096 --> 00:20:29,232
 he's telling them in their faces that, you are exhausted

278
00:20:29,256 --> 00:20:32,480
you are tired, you cannot carry on this fight forever.

279
00:20:33,149 --> 00:20:35,345
You see, they have been worn out.

280
00:20:36,443 --> 00:20:36,959
Then he said;

281
00:20:36,999 --> 00:20:41,031
 وَاُخْرَى اِنَّ رَسُوْلَ الله صلى الله عليه وَسلم يُخْبِرُكُمْ

282
00:20:41,186 --> 00:20:45,832
اَنَّه’لَمْ يَأت لِقِتَالِ اَحَدْ اِنَّمَا جَآءَ مُعْتَمِرًا

283
00:20:45,856 --> 00:20:49,607
معه الْهَدْي عَلَيْهِ الْقَلَائِدْ يَنْحرْه’ وَيَنْصَرِفْ

284
00:20:49,877 --> 00:20:53,482
Rasool Allah ﷺ telling you, he is informing you

285
00:20:53,506 --> 00:20:57,204
that we have not came here to fight anyone

286
00:20:57,228 --> 00:21:02,266
but we have come for Umrah(عمرة) with us the sacrificial animals marked,

287
00:21:02,603 --> 00:21:04,476
 we will slaughter them and leave.

288
00:21:05,510 --> 00:21:09,025
Abbaan Bin Saeed(عَبَّان بِن سَعيد) told Usman Bin Affan رضي الله عنه;

289
00:21:09,049 --> 00:21:11,733
If you want to make Tawaf(طواف) go ahead, no one can prevent you.

290
00:21:12,261 --> 00:21:13,808
What did Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) do?

291
00:21:14,265 --> 00:21:17,937
Actually some of the companions they were saying;

292
00:21:18,327 --> 00:21:20,381
Uthman(عثمان) is lucky, now is making Tawaf(طواف).

293
00:21:20,421 --> 00:21:22,617
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ heard them and said;

294
00:21:22,925 --> 00:21:28,171
My expectation of him, is that, if he stays so and so years,

295
00:21:28,918 --> 00:21:31,873
he would not make Tawaf(طواف) until, I make Tawaf(طواف)

296
00:21:32,411 --> 00:21:35,340
and that was the case Uthman Bin Affan رضي الله عنه said;

297
00:21:35,364 --> 00:21:38,486
مَا كُنْتُ لِأطُوْفَ بِالْبَيْتِ حَتَّى يَطُوْفَ بِهِ رسول الله

298
00:21:38,510 --> 00:21:41,680
I wouldn't have made Tawaf(طواف) around the house of Allah,

299
00:21:41,704 --> 00:21:44,700
until Rasool Allah ﷺ makes Tawaf(طواف) himself,

300
00:21:45,790 --> 00:21:49,687
out of respect to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

301
00:21:50,064 --> 00:21:55,011
Quraish(قريش) were also sending envoys the first they sent was Budail Bin Warqaa(بديل بن ورقاء).

302
00:21:55,360 --> 00:21:57,737
Budail Bin Warqaa(بديل بن ورقاء) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ

303
00:21:57,761 --> 00:22:01,408
and he belong to the tribe of Khuza'a(خزاعة) and he came along with some men from Khuza'a(خزاعة).

304
00:22:01,523 --> 00:22:03,236
As the books say,

305
00:22:03,619 --> 00:22:07,414
كَانُوْا عَيْبَة نُصْحِ لِرسُولِ صلى الله عليه وسلم

306
00:22:07,871 --> 00:22:12,687
They were trust worthy advisors of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

307
00:22:12,711 --> 00:22:14,254
مُشرِكْهِمْ وَكَافِرْهِمْ

308
00:22:14,375 --> 00:22:17,877
The disbelievers among them and the Muslims among them,

309
00:22:18,335 --> 00:22:20,580
were very sympathetic to the Muslims.

310
00:22:21,069 --> 00:22:25,015
And they were advisors of Rasool Allah ﷺ

311
00:22:25,039 --> 00:22:30,145
and it says in one narration that anything that goes on in Makkah

312
00:22:30,169 --> 00:22:33,064
the people of Khuza'a(خزاعة) would report it to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

313
00:22:33,858 --> 00:22:37,183
Rasool Allah ﷺ had information from within

314
00:22:37,207 --> 00:22:42,373
and the ones, who are bringing the information to Rasool Allah ﷺ were both Muslim and non Muslim.

315
00:22:42,892 --> 00:22:45,440
This was sort of like a tribal Alliance,

316
00:22:45,529 --> 00:22:50,139
because Khuza'a(خزاعة) were allies of Bannu Hashim(بنوهاشم) in the time of Jahilliyah(جاهلية).

317
00:22:50,272 --> 00:22:53,710
And since, the leader of Bannu Hashim(بنوهاشم) now, is Rasool Allah ﷺ

318
00:22:53,894 --> 00:22:56,159
he is the most prominent figure among them.

319
00:22:56,288 --> 00:23:01,751
Khuza'a(خزاعة) carried on this alliance, even though many of them were Mushrikeen(مشركين),

320
00:23:01,941 --> 00:23:08,012
 but they still considered themselves to be close to Bannu Hashim(بنوهاشم) and close to the Muslims.

321
00:23:08,497 --> 00:23:11,747
And this shows you the situation that existed then

322
00:23:12,095 --> 00:23:15,258
and there could be a lot of insight in this story.

323
00:23:15,598 --> 00:23:20,612
And in the relations between the clans and tribes that existed then

324
00:23:20,788 --> 00:23:24,518
and how Rasool Allah ﷺ was successful in his war.

325
00:23:24,967 --> 00:23:28,954
And one can also see that part of that success is

326
00:23:28,978 --> 00:23:32,040
because of his information gathering procedure

327
00:23:32,833 --> 00:23:39,631
always Rasool Allah ﷺ, had spies roaming Arabia to gather information for him

328
00:23:39,940 --> 00:23:42,717
and here we have insiders from within Makkah.

329
00:23:42,741 --> 00:23:45,736
Because Khuza'a(خزاعة) were living in the outskirts of Makkah, very close to Makkah

330
00:23:45,775 --> 00:23:50,808
and they would report to him whatever, was going on in the camp of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

331
00:23:51,695 --> 00:23:56,879
So, Budail Bin Warqaa(بديل بن ورقاء) was first envoy sent, to meet with Rasool Allah ﷺ

332
00:23:57,228 --> 00:24:00,303
He came to Muhammadﷺ and told him that Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

333
00:24:00,327 --> 00:24:04,307
مَعَهُمُ الْعُوْذ اَلْمَطافِيْلْ قَدْ نَزَّلُّ وعَدَدَ مَا اَلْحُدَيْبِيَه

334
00:24:04,451 --> 00:24:09,166
That Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) have came out, with them the camels with milk

335
00:24:09,513 --> 00:24:12,981
meaning that they have came out with provisions

336
00:24:13,567 --> 00:24:16,467
with the intention of staying for a long time,

337
00:24:16,877 --> 00:24:19,000
if the circumstances demand so

338
00:24:19,512 --> 00:24:21,167
and he told them they have.

339
00:24:21,191 --> 00:24:23,216
وَلَبِسُوْا جُلُوْدً النَّمُوْرَ،

340
00:24:23,391 --> 00:24:27,373
They have put on tiger skin and they're ready for war.

341
00:24:28,071 --> 00:24:29,466
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

342
00:24:30,275 --> 00:24:32,152
لَمْ نَجْيء لقِتَالِ اَحَدْ

343
00:24:32,586 --> 00:24:36,372
We did not come to fight anyone, we have come to make Umrah(عمرة).

344
00:24:36,861 --> 00:24:39,327
يَا وَيْحَ قُرَيْشٍ لَقَدْ اَنهِكتَهُمُ الْحَرْبَ

345
00:24:39,526 --> 00:24:41,985
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) have been consumed by warfare.

346
00:24:42,356 --> 00:24:43,727
It has ruined them.

347
00:24:44,012 --> 00:24:47,360
If they want, I will give them respite for a while.

348
00:24:47,677 --> 00:24:50,379
They should then give me access to the people,

349
00:24:50,719 --> 00:24:56,477
if I prevail and they wish to join into what the people have entered, they could do so.

350
00:24:56,748 --> 00:24:58,384
Otherwise, they will have rested

351
00:24:58,872 --> 00:25:03,715
if they refuse this, then I swear by Him, Who holds my soul in His hand,

352
00:25:03,739 --> 00:25:09,512
I will battle them in this cause of mine until, I perish and Allah's will, will be done.

353
00:25:10,399 --> 00:25:16,743
Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) you have the option of either leaving me alone

354
00:25:17,199 --> 00:25:20,718
or fighting me, and if you choose to fight me, I will win

355
00:25:21,014 --> 00:25:23,556
and Allah's religion will prevail

356
00:25:23,746 --> 00:25:28,341
and I'm not going to give up, I'm never going to give up, even if I perish.

357
00:25:29,165 --> 00:25:32,297
So, he is making it clear to them, that I'm not going to give up

358
00:25:32,645 --> 00:25:37,415
and Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling them that you have been exhausted by war.

359
00:25:37,951 --> 00:25:41,693
And we talked about earlier, Rasool Allah ﷺ said, after the battle of Khandaq(خندق),

360
00:25:41,717 --> 00:25:43,623
اَلْآنَ نَغْزُوهُمْ وَلاَ يَغْزُونَنَا

361
00:25:43,831 --> 00:25:47,412
We wil from now on conquer them and they will not conquer us.

362
00:25:47,443 --> 00:25:50,435
And that is what happened, Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) now are on the defensive.

363
00:25:51,034 --> 00:25:58,436
They have no ability to wage an offensive battle against Rasool Allah ﷺ.

364
00:25:58,800 --> 00:26:01,061
Budail Bin Warqaa(بديل بن ورقاء) told Rasool Ullah I'm going to tell them,

365
00:26:01,085 --> 00:26:02,816
I'm going to convey to them, this message

366
00:26:02,840 --> 00:26:06,217
Budail Bin Warqaa(بديل بن ورقاء) went back to Makkah

367
00:26:06,877 --> 00:26:08,382
and the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) said;

368
00:26:08,660 --> 00:26:12,719
He wants you to ask him, what happened, ignore him.

369
00:26:13,038 --> 00:26:16,035
So, Budail(بديل) came in and he's waiting for someone to ask him

370
00:26:16,484 --> 00:26:20,291
what happened and they were all quiet, so he told them;

371
00:26:20,803 --> 00:26:23,666
He told them: Do you want me to tell you what happened.

372
00:26:24,303 --> 00:26:27,841
Ikrimah Bin Abi Jahal(عِكْرِمَة بن ابي جهل) said: We don't want to hear anything from you.

373
00:26:28,157 --> 00:26:30,891
They knew his sympathy towards the Muslims.

374
00:26:31,168 --> 00:26:33,304
But then Safwaan Ibn Umayyah(صفوان اِبن أمَيَّة) and some others, they said;

375
00:26:33,344 --> 00:26:34,509
 Go ahead and tell us what happened.

376
00:26:34,540 --> 00:26:37,359
He convey to them the message of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

377
00:26:38,137 --> 00:26:39,490
They didn't like what they heard.

378
00:26:41,097 --> 00:26:43,236
So, now they sent in, another man.

379
00:26:43,664 --> 00:26:46,985
This time they sent, a man called Mikraz Bin Hafz(مكرزبن حفص).

380
00:26:47,481 --> 00:26:49,107
When Rasool Allah ﷺ saw him. He said;

381
00:26:49,131 --> 00:26:50,585
اِنَّ هَذَا رَجُلٌ غَادِر

382
00:26:50,609 --> 00:26:52,649
This is a man of the betrayal

383
00:26:53,161 --> 00:26:55,178
and why did Rasool Allah ﷺ say that about him?

384
00:26:55,202 --> 00:26:56,394
Rasool Allah knew his nature.

385
00:26:56,440 --> 00:27:02,228
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) after that he led a force of 40 or 50 men from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

386
00:27:02,412 --> 00:27:06,118
with the intention of circling around the Muslim camp,

387
00:27:06,190 --> 00:27:11,662
 trying to find any loner to take as prisoner.

388
00:27:12,037 --> 00:27:15,708
They wanted to find anybody who would deviate away from the army

389
00:27:15,748 --> 00:27:19,864
 and they would capture him and take him back to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

390
00:27:19,958 --> 00:27:22,633
What happened is the other way around.

391
00:27:22,821 --> 00:27:26,799
It was the Muslims, who took them as prisoners, all of them, except Mikraz(مِكْرَز) who ran away.

392
00:27:27,150 --> 00:27:30,305
They came in, to take prisoners and they were taken prisoners themselves.

393
00:27:30,375 --> 00:27:33,477
Rasool Allah ﷺ because he came out, with the intension of peace

394
00:27:33,571 --> 00:27:36,071
he released them all, with no condition.

395
00:27:36,696 --> 00:27:41,628
Then Al-Hulais Bin Alqama(اَلْحُلَيْس بن عَلْقَمَة), the head of Al-Ahabeesh(اَلْاَحَابِيْش),

396
00:27:42,151 --> 00:27:43,338
these are the Allies of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

397
00:27:43,393 --> 00:27:46,711
 He offered to go and meet with Rasool Allah ﷺ

398
00:27:46,870 --> 00:27:51,198
when Rasool Allah ﷺ saw him, he said: This is a man from people who are devout

399
00:27:51,683 --> 00:27:56,609
drive out the animals of sacrifice in front of him so he will see them.

400
00:27:56,929 --> 00:28:00,066
So, the Muslims all what they had to do is,

401
00:28:00,106 --> 00:28:04,785
to show out their intentions of Umrah(عمرة) publicly

402
00:28:05,375 --> 00:28:08,590
and this man as soon as he saw that

403
00:28:08,913 --> 00:28:12,387
he walked away without even meeting with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

404
00:28:13,158 --> 00:28:15,456
He was so moved, by what he saw

405
00:28:15,859 --> 00:28:18,094
he went back to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and said;

406
00:28:18,119 --> 00:28:20,182
All glory belongs to Allah,

407
00:28:20,252 --> 00:28:23,559
it is not right for these people to be kept from Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

408
00:28:23,765 --> 00:28:25,364
and this is a Mushrik(مشرك) a Kafir(كافر).

409
00:28:25,547 --> 00:28:29,739
But he saw it, is against the tradition, against the acceptable norms, of the time

410
00:28:30,050 --> 00:28:34,335
to prevent people who came out for Umrah(عمرة) to prevent them from entering in the house of Allah.

411
00:28:35,198 --> 00:28:35,972
It's like, he is saying,

412
00:28:36,012 --> 00:28:40,267
I mean, Who are you, people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) to prevent, the people from coming into Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)?

413
00:28:40,404 --> 00:28:42,629
And then in another narration, he said;

414
00:28:42,654 --> 00:28:48,344
اَبَى اللهُ اَنْ تَحُجَّ لَخَمْ وَجُدَام وكِنْده َوَحِمْيَرْ وَيُمْنَعْ مِنْهَا اِبْنَ عَبْدَالْمُطُلِبْ

415
00:28:48,597 --> 00:28:56,243
Allah will not allow Lakham(لَخَم), and Judaam(جُذَام), and Himyar(حِمْيَر), and Kindaa(كِنْدَةْ) to come and visit the house of Allah,

416
00:28:56,401 --> 00:28:59,309
while the son of Abdul-Muttalib(عبدالمطلب) himself is prevented.

417
00:28:59,334 --> 00:29:02,860
These four tribes he mentioned belong to the Yemeni branch of the Arabs

418
00:29:02,885 --> 00:29:04,819
Al-Qahtaniyien(ألقحطانيين), that’s one thing

419
00:29:05,070 --> 00:29:07,774
and the second is that they live in the furthest parts of Arabia.

420
00:29:07,799 --> 00:29:13,149
Lakham(لَخَم), and Judaam(جُذَام) they live to the extreme north of Arabia in Ash-Sham(ألشام)

421
00:29:13,266 --> 00:29:18,612
and then Kindaa(كِنْدَةْ) and Himyar(حِمْيَر) to the extreme south, in the southern parts of Yemen

422
00:29:19,102 --> 00:29:20,135
and he is telling them;

423
00:29:20,222 --> 00:29:25,588
 These tribes are allowed to come and visit the house of Allah,

424
00:29:25,723 --> 00:29:30,612
while the son of Abdul-Muttalib(عبدالمطلب), who are from the people of Adnan(عدنان), the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

425
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:33,194
and he is from Makkah itself.

426
00:29:33,471 --> 00:29:36,539
You prevent him and he was very angry

427
00:29:36,839 --> 00:29:38,575
and the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) told him:

428
00:29:38,615 --> 00:29:41,408
Just sit down, you are a Bedouin without any sense.

429
00:29:41,557 --> 00:29:43,806
Al-Hullais(اَلْحُلَيْس) was very angry with that and said;

430
00:29:43,877 --> 00:29:48,502
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) it wasn't for this, that we are allied with you and have a pact with you

431
00:29:48,573 --> 00:29:52,526
shall someone who has come to venerate Allah's house, be barred from it

432
00:29:52,620 --> 00:29:55,143
by Him who holds the soul of Al-Hullais(اَلْحُلَيْس)

433
00:29:55,427 --> 00:29:58,430
either you allow Muhammad(محمد) to do what he has come for

434
00:29:58,567 --> 00:30:02,000
or I will mobilize the Al-Ahabeesh(اَلْاَحَابِيْش) to the last man of them.

435
00:30:02,544 --> 00:30:06,737
He threaten them with war and then the people Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) have calmed him down and said;

436
00:30:06,826 --> 00:30:10,841
Keep silent and leave us alone, until we get for ourselves, what we want.

437
00:30:10,938 --> 00:30:12,555
They're just trying to save face.

438
00:30:13,677 --> 00:30:15,620
All of the envoys were a failure.

439
00:30:16,186 --> 00:30:20,143
Then Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَةبن مسعود), he came to them and said to the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

440
00:30:20,741 --> 00:30:23,118
اَلَسْتُم بِالْوَالِدْ واَلَسْتٌ بِالْوَلَدْ

441
00:30:23,548 --> 00:30:26,519
Aren't you my parents

442
00:30:26,839 --> 00:30:30,331
or aren't you the ones, who have given birth to me and I'm your son,

443
00:30:30,658 --> 00:30:34,530
Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَةبن مسعود), he is from the tribe Thaqeef(ثقيف), who come from At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف).

444
00:30:34,799 --> 00:30:37,899
But his mother was from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

445
00:30:38,678 --> 00:30:41,475
and he was one of the great men of Arabia.

446
00:30:41,500 --> 00:30:46,059
In fact, he was one of the suggested names when the Mushrikeen(مشركين) said;

447
00:30:46,210 --> 00:30:50,402
لَوْلَا نُزِّلَ هَٰذَا الْقُرْآنُ عَلَىٰ رَجُلٍ مِنَ الْقَرْيَتَيْنِ عَظِيمٍ۝

448
00:30:50,623 --> 00:30:57,020
Why wasn't this book revealed on one of the great men of the two towns.

449
00:30:57,060 --> 00:31:00,051
They were referring to Makkah and At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف)

450
00:31:00,293 --> 00:31:01,934
So, the Mushrikeen(مشركين) were saying;

451
00:31:01,974 --> 00:31:05,086
Why did Allah chose Muhammad(محمد), why didn't He chose Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود)?

452
00:31:05,567 --> 00:31:06,926
So he was an important figure.

453
00:31:07,328 --> 00:31:10,185
He came to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and he saw that all of this wasn't making sense.

454
00:31:10,518 --> 00:31:12,790
So, he told them; I'm your son.

455
00:31:13,060 --> 00:31:16,353
 Do you want me to go and see this man? They said: Yes.

456
00:31:16,734 --> 00:31:17,606
But then I told them;

457
00:31:17,646 --> 00:31:24,620
I have seen all of the insults you have poured on the heads of the people who went as envoys for you.

458
00:31:24,660 --> 00:31:26,073
I mean, whenever one would come back,

459
00:31:26,153 --> 00:31:30,609
whether it is a Al-Hullais(اَلْحُلَيْس) or Budail Bin Warqaa(بديل بن ورقاء), they would insult them

460
00:31:30,631 --> 00:31:32,800
they send them and then they insult them, when they come back

461
00:31:32,822 --> 00:31:36,742
 because they come back with an answer different than, what they want to hear.

462
00:31:36,948 --> 00:31:40,513
So, Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود) doesn't want the same thing to happen to them.

463
00:31:40,743 --> 00:31:43,901
They said: We trust you and go and speak to him.

464
00:31:44,195 --> 00:31:49,195
So, Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود), he went to Muhammadﷺ and he said;

465
00:31:49,544 --> 00:31:55,595
 Hey, now Muhammad(محمد), haven't you considered that you are ruining, your own people?

466
00:31:55,902 --> 00:32:00,853
Have you have heard of any Arab who ruined his people before yourself?

467
00:32:01,678 --> 00:32:07,081
And if that does not happen, I swear, I do not see faces here.

468
00:32:07,453 --> 00:32:13,220
I just see a hodgepodge of people who are quite capable of fleeing and abandoning you.

469
00:32:13,927 --> 00:32:20,225
Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود) is mentioning to Rasool Allah ﷺ the two options that he sees;

470
00:32:20,714 --> 00:32:25,351
The first option, is that you win by ruining your own people

471
00:32:25,888 --> 00:32:29,984
then he told him, have you ever seen an Arab man who ruined his own tribe.

472
00:32:30,009 --> 00:32:33,061
This is a tribal society, the tribe is everything

473
00:32:33,475 --> 00:32:38,256
and the way Urwa(عُروة) sees it is that Muhammadﷺ is invading his own people.

474
00:32:39,189 --> 00:32:40,639
And this is unacceptable.

475
00:32:40,886 --> 00:32:45,234
And we haven't heard of anyone who has done such a thing before you.

476
00:32:45,507 --> 00:32:46,857
I mean, he's trying to tell him;

477
00:32:47,194 --> 00:32:51,170
This is a disgrace and this is a shameful thing to do, so don't do it.

478
00:32:51,517 --> 00:32:54,146
And the other option is that you will be defeated.

479
00:32:54,908 --> 00:32:58,156
And he sees this as a likely option because he said;

480
00:32:58,324 --> 00:33:00,042
فَاِنِيْ اَرَاَءْ اَوْبَاشًا

481
00:33:00,789 --> 00:33:01,740
And in another narration;

482
00:33:01,780 --> 00:33:06,383
 اَشْوَابًا مِنَّ النَاسْ يُوْشِك اَنْ يَّفِرُّوْ وَيَدَعُوْكْ

483
00:33:06,639 --> 00:33:08,592
I see a hodgepodge of people.

484
00:33:09,143 --> 00:33:13,131
What he is referring to is that, the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم are from different tribes.

485
00:33:13,156 --> 00:33:18,340
They belong to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they belong to Al-Aos(ألأوس), Al-Khazraj(اَلْخَزرَج), Aslam(اَسْلَم), Ghifaar(غِفَار).

486
00:33:18,971 --> 00:33:22,951
And for some of these tribes like, Aslam(اَسْلَم) and Ghifaar(غِفَار)

487
00:33:23,439 --> 00:33:29,189
they were seen by, by people like Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود) as being second class tribes.

488
00:33:29,214 --> 00:33:33,494
I mean, you have the major tribes of the Thaqeef(ثقيف) and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

489
00:33:33,700 --> 00:33:36,738
and then you have these smaller tribes like Aslam(اَسْلَم) and Ghifaar(غِفَار).

490
00:33:37,203 --> 00:33:41,852
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), the larger tribes were slow in accepting Islam

491
00:33:42,287 --> 00:33:44,405
because of their arrogance and pride

492
00:33:45,222 --> 00:33:48,675
and they felt that Islam will take away their position of prominence.

493
00:33:49,178 --> 00:33:53,781
However, these smaller tribes were more willing to listen to the truth

494
00:33:54,255 --> 00:33:57,085
because these barriers were not ahead of them.

495
00:33:57,555 --> 00:34:00,327
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says in Hadith(حديث)

496
00:34:00,597 --> 00:34:05,002
that these tribes are better than Tamim(تميم) and Ghatafaan(غطفان) and Asad(أسد)

497
00:34:05,050 --> 00:34:07,394
 you know these big tribes, who people look up to.

498
00:34:07,643 --> 00:34:08,635
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

499
00:34:08,660 --> 00:34:13,976
On the Day of Judgment these smaller tribes like Mazeena(مَزِيْنَة) and Juhaynah(جهينة) and Aslam(اسلم) and Ghaffar(غفار)

500
00:34:14,256 --> 00:34:19,911
are heavier on the scale on the Day of Judgment then Tamim(تميم) and Asad(أسد) and Ghatafaan(غطافان) and their likes.

501
00:34:21,062 --> 00:34:26,648
But the Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود) was viewing things from the tribal Jahilliyah(جاهلية) view

502
00:34:26,971 --> 00:34:31,547
and he said: What I see is a hodgepodge, a mob of people

503
00:34:31,998 --> 00:34:36,279
that when things get serious, when the rubber hits the road, they're going to leave you alone

504
00:34:36,304 --> 00:34:38,692
they're going to flee and leave you alone.

505
00:34:39,117 --> 00:34:44,053
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) when he heard that, he saw this as a great insult that would not go unnoticed.

506
00:34:44,078 --> 00:34:50,403
So, he told him: Go and suck on Laat(لات)'s clitoris, would we flee and abandon him.?

507
00:34:50,798 --> 00:34:52,212
This was a big insult.

508
00:34:52,498 --> 00:34:56,895
The Arabs used to insult each other, this was a curse among them,

509
00:34:57,201 --> 00:35:00,773
they would say suck on your mother's clitoris,

510
00:35:00,813 --> 00:35:03,312
excuse me for using these words,

511
00:35:03,352 --> 00:35:07,461
but this is knowledge that is mentioned in the books and

512
00:35:07,590 --> 00:35:08,606
 لَا اَحْيَآء فِيْ الدِّيْنْ

513
00:35:08,646 --> 00:35:10,215
 There is no shame in religion,

514
00:35:10,424 --> 00:35:14,956
we're just narrating what is mentioned in the books of Seerah(سيرة).

515
00:35:15,510 --> 00:35:20,159
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) changed it here and replaced mother with Al-Laat(ألات)

516
00:35:20,334 --> 00:35:23,580
and Al-Laat(ألات) was the major god of the people of the Thaqeef(ثقيف).

517
00:35:23,605 --> 00:35:27,970
So, it was a great insult on Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود) to tell him this.

518
00:35:28,618 --> 00:35:32,258
Urwa(عُرْوَة) he stared at Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and told him;

519
00:35:32,598 --> 00:35:36,300
If it wasn't because of your favor towards me,

520
00:35:36,616 --> 00:35:42,997
I would have responded back but, I will stay quiet and by this I have paid you back your favor.

521
00:35:43,635 --> 00:35:49,902
Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود) was referring to the fact that once he was responsible for paying blood money

522
00:35:50,212 --> 00:35:52,071
 and Blood Money is 100 camels.

523
00:35:52,310 --> 00:35:56,088
So, he called people, his friends to help him out.

524
00:35:56,515 --> 00:36:01,951
And people will help him out with one camel, two camels, three camels, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) helped him out with 10.

525
00:36:02,229 --> 00:36:03,464
This is in the time of Jahilliyah(جاهلية).

526
00:36:03,504 --> 00:36:05,119
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was a very generous man.

527
00:36:05,271 --> 00:36:10,334
And the insult was so great that Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَةبن مسعود) saw that

528
00:36:10,397 --> 00:36:15,736
 he has paid back Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) for his favor of giving him 10 camels

529
00:36:15,815 --> 00:36:19,403
 by just remaining silent and not responding back to him

530
00:36:19,443 --> 00:36:23,093
 because this was a big curse to Al-Laat(ألات)

531
00:36:23,585 --> 00:36:28,958
but Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) his temper could not handle such a comment by Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَةبن مسعود)

532
00:36:28,998 --> 00:36:33,157
to say that the Muslims are going to flee and leave Rasool Allah ﷺ alone.

533
00:36:33,622 --> 00:36:34,559
Brothers and Sisters,

534
00:36:34,618 --> 00:36:40,384
what kind of impression does the actions of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم give the Kuffar(كفار),

535
00:36:40,715 --> 00:36:45,153
when they see their solidarity, and they see their strength

536
00:36:45,592 --> 00:36:49,636
and they see their willingness, to sacrifice for Rasool Allah ﷺ.

537
00:36:49,813 --> 00:36:55,713
No watered down message, no weakness, when it comes to the defense of Rasool Allah ﷺ

538
00:36:55,920 --> 00:36:58,636
we're gonna fight for him and we're never going to leave him alone.

539
00:36:59,086 --> 00:37:02,068
And then Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود) when he would speak to Rasool Allah ﷺ

540
00:37:02,093 --> 00:37:05,776
he would extend his hand to hold his beard

541
00:37:05,829 --> 00:37:11,130
 and this was something that people would do in those days when they would talk with each other.

542
00:37:11,644 --> 00:37:16,784
It was something acceptable but here Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود) is talking with who?

543
00:37:16,921 --> 00:37:18,653
He is talking with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

544
00:37:18,708 --> 00:37:20,670
So, whenever he would extend his hand

545
00:37:20,931 --> 00:37:26,074
Al-Mugheerah Bin Sho'ba(ألمغيره بن شعبة) who was standing next to Rasool Allah ﷺ to guard him,

546
00:37:26,114 --> 00:37:27,679
while Rasool Allah ﷺ sitting down

547
00:37:27,740 --> 00:37:30,388
and Al-Mugheera(اَلْمُغِيْرَة) had his sword in his hand,

548
00:37:30,663 --> 00:37:38,866
he would strike the hand of Urwa(عُرْوَةْ) with the handle of his sword and would tell him;

549
00:37:39,133 --> 00:37:42,108
Keep your hand away from Rasool Allah ﷺ

550
00:37:42,261 --> 00:37:44,925
otherwise, it's not going to return back to you.

551
00:37:45,276 --> 00:37:46,728
I'm going to cut it off.

552
00:37:47,304 --> 00:37:51,592
Al-Mugheera(اَلْمُغِيْرَة) was covered in armor from head to toe

553
00:37:51,924 --> 00:37:54,133
and only his eyes could be seen.

554
00:37:54,360 --> 00:37:56,941
So, Urwa(عُرْوَةْ) did not know, who this man was?

555
00:37:57,226 --> 00:38:00,019
So, he told Rasool Allah ﷺ, in one narration

556
00:38:00,282 --> 00:38:01,746
مَا اَفَضكَ وَاَغْلَظَكْ

557
00:38:02,015 --> 00:38:03,588
How rough and rude you are?

558
00:38:03,873 --> 00:38:06,257
And in another narration, he told Rasool Allah ﷺ;

559
00:38:06,282 --> 00:38:10,593
I don't think there's any man more wicked than this man in your army.

560
00:38:10,741 --> 00:38:11,527
Who is he?

561
00:38:11,725 --> 00:38:16,909
Rasool Allah ﷺ smiled and said: This is your nephew Al-Mugheerah Bin Sho'ba(ألمغيره بن شعبة).

562
00:38:17,116 --> 00:38:20,016
Al-Mugheera(اَلْمُغِيْرَة) was the nephew of Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود),

563
00:38:20,041 --> 00:38:23,258
what a surprise it would be to Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود) to see

564
00:38:23,312 --> 00:38:27,667
that the man who was roughest with him, was his own nephew

565
00:38:28,194 --> 00:38:32,879
and then Urwa(عُرْوَةْ) said: Oh You wicked man, or you man of betrayal;

566
00:38:33,192 --> 00:38:38,034
Have I not just washed away your betrayal yesterday?

567
00:38:38,265 --> 00:38:40,483
What Urwa(عُرْوَةْ) is referring to here,

568
00:38:40,523 --> 00:38:47,546
Al-Mugheerah Bin Sho'ba(ألمغيره بن شعبة) in the time of Jahilliyah(جاهليه) he traveled with 13 Mushrikeen(مُشركين)

569
00:38:48,007 --> 00:38:55,122
and he killed them all stole their money and then ran away to Madina to become Muslim.

570
00:38:55,617 --> 00:39:01,693
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: I will accept Islam from you but, I will not accept this money.

571
00:39:02,369 --> 00:39:07,022
Because there was trust among these travelers and he betrayed them and took their money.

572
00:39:07,252 --> 00:39:09,778
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I want nothing to do with this money.

573
00:39:09,884 --> 00:39:14,702
Rasool Ullah did not paid back to the Mushrikeen(مُشركين), he did not apologize to the Mushrikeen(مُشركين)

574
00:39:15,518 --> 00:39:17,829
but in the same time he refused to accept it

575
00:39:18,200 --> 00:39:20,240
because the way it was taken wasn't right.

576
00:39:20,815 --> 00:39:23,452
Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود) was the one, who had to pay it

577
00:39:24,019 --> 00:39:26,027
being the relative of Al-Mugheera(اَلْمُغِيْرَة).

578
00:39:26,242 --> 00:39:32,536
And he also had to pay the blood money for all of these men whom Al-Mugheerah Bin Sho'ba(ألمغيره بن شعبة) killed.

579
00:39:33,010 --> 00:39:34,209
So, he's telling Al-Mugheera(اَلْمُغِيْرَة),

580
00:39:34,249 --> 00:39:40,257
I just took care of your betrayal and this is how you treat me.

581
00:39:40,473 --> 00:39:45,890
So, you can see brothers and sisters how Islam changed the hearts of these men

582
00:39:45,915 --> 00:39:53,550
and how their love of Rasool Allah ﷺ, they would put it ahead of any personal needs or personal relations,

583
00:39:53,710 --> 00:39:59,052
you know, because Al-Mugheera(اَلْمُغِيْرَة) here was helped by his uncle

584
00:39:59,455 --> 00:40:02,764
and at least he should have felt gratitude for that

585
00:40:02,804 --> 00:40:05,390
but his love of Rasool Allah ﷺ, was so great,

586
00:40:05,921 --> 00:40:08,614
that he dealt with Urwa(عُرْوَةْ) in such a manner

587
00:40:08,749 --> 00:40:12,984
because he saw him as being disrespectful with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

588
00:40:13,009 --> 00:40:20,296
And I see the statement of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and the action of Al-Mugheera(اَلْمُغِيْرَة) as amazing examples

589
00:40:20,629 --> 00:40:23,976
of how the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم loved Rasool Allah ﷺ.

590
00:40:24,488 --> 00:40:27,732
And sometimes you might not appreciate this, brothers and sisters

591
00:40:27,924 --> 00:40:30,425
until, you put yourself in their shoes,

592
00:40:30,465 --> 00:40:33,291
 until you start to think the way, they were thinking

593
00:40:33,331 --> 00:40:39,632
and to put yourself in those circumstances and to see how difficult it would be to act in such a way

594
00:40:39,807 --> 00:40:45,723
unless you have a very deep and sincere love of Rasool Ullah صلواة الله وسلام عليه.

595
00:40:46,405 --> 00:40:50,262
Ibn-e-Hajar(اِبْنِ حَجَر) he comments on the statement of Urwa(عُرْوَةْ)

596
00:40:50,656 --> 00:40:52,609
when he said, that you have two options,

597
00:40:52,634 --> 00:40:56,488
one is to fight your people and defeat them and you would ruin your people then

598
00:40:56,777 --> 00:41:01,740
or your followers would leave you alone and then you would be taken as prisoner.

599
00:41:02,533 --> 00:41:03,291
Ibn-e-Hajar(اِبْنِ حَجَر) says;

600
00:41:03,331 --> 00:41:09,324
وَالْحَاصِلْ اَنَّ عُرْوَةْ رَدَّدَ الْاَمْرَ بَيْنَ شَّيئيْنْ غَيْرَ مسْتَحْسَنَيْنَ عَادَةً

601
00:41:09,640 --> 00:41:11,885
وَهُوَ هَلَاكُ قَوْمِهِ اِنْ غَلَبْ

602
00:41:12,585 --> 00:41:14,852
وَذھابُ اَصْحَابِهِ اِنْ غُلِبْ

603
00:41:15,247 --> 00:41:22,302
لَكِنْ كُلٌ مِّنَّ الْأمرَيْنْ مُسْتَحْسَنٌ شَرْعًا كَمَا قَالَ تعَالَى

604
00:41:22,463 --> 00:41:25,263
قُلْ هَلْ تَرَبَّصُونَ بِنَا إِلَّا إِحْدَى الْحُسْنَيَيْنِ ۖ

605
00:41:25,668 --> 00:41:32,511
Urwa(عُرْوَةْ) he saw the two options as being disliked because of the norms,

606
00:41:32,844 --> 00:41:36,216
the first is the defeat of his people, if he wins

607
00:41:36,516 --> 00:41:41,040
and the fleeing away of his companions if he loses.

608
00:41:41,302 --> 00:41:48,266
However, both of these options are praised Shar'an(شَرْعاً) in Islam.

609
00:41:48,989 --> 00:41:52,172
Islam changes the way, we look at things.

610
00:41:52,711 --> 00:41:57,832
Our norms, our traditions our view changes because of Islam.

611
00:41:58,152 --> 00:41:59,631
So, Ibn-e-Hajar(اِبْنِ حَجَر) is saying,

612
00:41:59,830 --> 00:42:04,631
that if Rasool Allah ﷺ defeated his people, that is something, that is praised in Shar'iah(شرية)

613
00:42:04,854 --> 00:42:08,844
even though, it is his own tribe because it is  Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

614
00:42:09,051 --> 00:42:15,757
And if Rasool Allah ﷺ loses, than it is something that is also praiseworthy because it is Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

615
00:42:15,910 --> 00:42:17,340
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

616
00:42:17,587 --> 00:42:20,414
قُلْ هَلْ تَرَبَّصُونَ بِنَا إِلَّا إِحْدَى الْحُسْنَيَيْنِ ۖ

617
00:42:20,605 --> 00:42:23,890
Allah is telling the Muslims to tell the disbelievers that;

618
00:42:24,300 --> 00:42:26,612
What are you waiting for, to happen to us?

619
00:42:26,766 --> 00:42:30,965
Both are good for us, if we win, or we lose.

620
00:42:31,325 --> 00:42:34,768
Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَةبن مسعود) had an experience of a lifetime.

621
00:42:34,966 --> 00:42:37,589
He went back to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), and what did he say? He said:

622
00:42:37,921 --> 00:42:40,653
Well, I have gone into kings

623
00:42:41,509 --> 00:42:46,814
I had audiences with cesar, Khasro(خُسْرَو) and the Nagis,

624
00:42:47,240 --> 00:42:49,340
and I swear by a Allah

625
00:42:49,493 --> 00:42:53,962
I've never seen the subjects of any King venerate him

626
00:42:54,137 --> 00:42:56,850
the way, Muhammad(محمد)'s people venerate him.

627
00:42:57,014 --> 00:43:02,232
I swear, if he spits, the phelgem always falls into the palm of one of them,

628
00:43:02,272 --> 00:43:05,832
 and he would then rub it on to his face or skin.

629
00:43:05,912 --> 00:43:09,404
If he gives them a command, they hurry to carry it out.

630
00:43:09,471 --> 00:43:12,934
If he speaks, they lower their voices in his presence

631
00:43:13,103 --> 00:43:18,053
and they never look directly at him, out of their veneration for him

632
00:43:18,108 --> 00:43:20,702
he has made you an offer, so accept it.

633
00:43:21,701 --> 00:43:23,294
And according to Az-zohri(ألزهري), he said;

634
00:43:23,487 --> 00:43:27,996
I've seen a people, who would never abandon him for any reason.

635
00:43:28,060 --> 00:43:29,964
So, draw your own conclusions.

636
00:43:30,252 --> 00:43:33,160
He came with some ideas, but they were changed

637
00:43:33,303 --> 00:43:36,797
when he saw the reality of the situation in front of his eyes.

638
00:43:37,311 --> 00:43:38,933
When Rasool Ullah would make Wudho'o(وضؤ),

639
00:43:39,028 --> 00:43:45,503
the Sahabah(صحابه) would rush to pick up the droplets of water that would fall down from Rasool Allah ﷺ

640
00:43:45,528 --> 00:43:49,224
and, they would rub it on their skin to get the blessing from Rasool Allah ﷺ.

641
00:43:49,310 --> 00:43:52,145
If a hair falls down, they would take it and they would hide it.

642
00:43:52,751 --> 00:43:56,445
If he would spits, they would take that and Rub it onto themselves.

643
00:43:56,621 --> 00:44:02,121
They saw that everything that had to do with Rasool Allah ﷺ

644
00:44:02,160 --> 00:44:04,680
had the blessings of Rasool Allah ﷺ in it.

645
00:44:05,888 --> 00:44:10,157
This was their respect and love for Rasool Allah ﷺ.

646
00:44:10,271 --> 00:44:15,845
Urwa Bin Masood(عُروَة بن مسعود) is seasoned man, this leader from among his society

647
00:44:15,870 --> 00:44:19,041
the man who has traveled the world and met with the kings

648
00:44:19,081 --> 00:44:24,546
and has met with the greatest kings of the time Qaesar(قيصر) and Kisraa(كِسرى) and An-Najjashi(اَلنَّجَّاشي).

649
00:44:24,636 --> 00:44:28,032
He said: I have never seen something like what I saw in Hudaybiyyah(حديبية).

650
00:44:28,398 --> 00:44:31,335
He was amazed, he was surprised, later on, he would become Muslim.

651
00:44:32,027 --> 00:44:33,994
He was surprised by what he saw.

652
00:44:34,521 --> 00:44:38,141
See brothers or sisters; This is the living example of Da'wah(دعوة)

653
00:44:38,372 --> 00:44:41,160
not the Da'wah(دعوة) of words But the Da'wah(دعوة) of actions.

654
00:44:41,367 --> 00:44:45,492
We need Da'wah(دعوة) of words, but we need Da'wah(دعوة) of actions to confirm it.

655
00:44:46,145 --> 00:44:51,292
Urwa(عُرْوَةْ) has heard the Da'wah(دعوة) of words but now, he saw it with his own eyes.

656
00:44:52,047 --> 00:44:56,683
He saw the embodiment of the Da'wah(دعوة) of the Islam, in front of his eyes.

657
00:44:58,159 --> 00:45:02,797
He told the people of Quraish(قريش), Muhammadﷺ has given you an offer accept it.

658
00:45:03,240 --> 00:45:05,267
There's no way, you could defeat these people.

659
00:45:06,225 --> 00:45:10,040
I don't see any hope for you, he has given you an offer take it.

660
00:45:10,661 --> 00:45:13,014
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) was still in Makkah

661
00:45:13,533 --> 00:45:18,468
and a rumor spread, its time of war, so it's time of rumors.

662
00:45:19,073 --> 00:45:21,384
A rumor spread that he has been killed.

663
00:45:21,958 --> 00:45:26,365
Rasool Allah ﷺ headed towards the campground of Bannu Najjar(بنونجَّار),

664
00:45:26,390 --> 00:45:30,217
every clan had its own camping ground.

665
00:45:30,776 --> 00:45:35,266
Umm Ammarah رضي الله عنها, this woman from among Bannu Najjar(بنونجَّار).

666
00:45:35,700 --> 00:45:39,904
She said: I saw Rasool Allah ﷺ heading towards our tents.

667
00:45:40,019 --> 00:45:41,879
So, I thought that he needed something

668
00:45:42,429 --> 00:45:45,436
he came and sat down and said;

669
00:45:45,508 --> 00:45:47,952
 اِنَّ الله اَمَرَنِيْ بالْبَيْعَهْ

670
00:45:48,351 --> 00:45:54,095
Allah has commanded me to take the pledge from the Muslims

671
00:45:54,895 --> 00:45:59,167
and he asked first man to give him Bay'ah(بيعة)

672
00:45:59,624 --> 00:46:03,033
and then the Muslim started rushing to give him Bay'ah(بيعة).

673
00:46:03,272 --> 00:46:06,605
What was the Bay'ah(بيعة) for, what were the terms of the Bay'ah(بيعة)?

674
00:46:06,714 --> 00:46:10,360
In one narration, to die, we pledge to die,

675
00:46:10,693 --> 00:46:15,955
the other narration, we pledge not to flee from battle

676
00:46:16,178 --> 00:46:17,511
and the third narration,

677
00:46:17,638 --> 00:46:19,768
 نُبَايِعُكَ عَلَى مَا فِيْ نَفْسِكْ

678
00:46:20,012 --> 00:46:24,464
We pledge to you, according to what is in your heart.

679
00:46:24,918 --> 00:46:29,412
And this last narration is amazing that the Sahabah(صحابه) are willing to pledge,

680
00:46:29,546 --> 00:46:33,491
whatever is in the heart of Rasool Allah ﷺ we'll pledge to it.

681
00:46:33,571 --> 00:46:35,040
Even if, I don't know

682
00:46:35,120 --> 00:46:38,171
 and in fact one can take from these three narrations

683
00:46:38,251 --> 00:46:41,960
that the Sahabah(صحابه) maybe Allah-Ho-Alam(الله اعلم), this could be derived from this.

684
00:46:42,115 --> 00:46:45,404
They weren't sure exactly, what the pledge for

685
00:46:45,444 --> 00:46:51,632
but they were still pledging because whatever Rasool Allah ﷺ would ask from them, they would do.

686
00:46:52,221 --> 00:46:54,860
Also we can see that the meaning is similar between

687
00:46:55,003 --> 00:46:57,140
الموت و ان لا نفر

688
00:46:57,165 --> 00:46:59,150
To die and not to flee from battle.

689
00:46:59,270 --> 00:47:02,746
This was the Bay'ah(بيعة) of Ar-Ridhwaan(الرضوان)

690
00:47:02,833 --> 00:47:04,815
is called the Bay'ah(بيعة) of the pleasure of Allah.

691
00:47:04,855 --> 00:47:08,100
 Allah was pleased with the Muslims after this Bay'ah(بيعة).

692
00:47:08,267 --> 00:47:09,450
Why did they give the Bay'ah(بيعة)?

693
00:47:09,577 --> 00:47:13,880
 It is because of the rumor that Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) has been killed.

694
00:47:14,405 --> 00:47:17,627
Now, before we proceed, few things regarding this Bay'ah(بيعة);

695
00:47:17,951 --> 00:47:21,457
The Bay'ah(بيعة) was done in the camp of Bannu Najjar(بنونجَّار).

696
00:47:21,497 --> 00:47:22,862
So, who are Bannu Najjar(بنونجَّار)?

697
00:47:23,083 --> 00:47:26,664
Bannu Najjar(بنونجَّار) belongs the tribe of Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج)

698
00:47:27,129 --> 00:47:32,550
and they are the maternal uncles of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

699
00:47:32,591 --> 00:47:36,318
If you remember, if you go back to the Makkah period, we talked about that.

700
00:47:36,844 --> 00:47:43,850
And they were like the close associates and private soldiers of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

701
00:47:43,924 --> 00:47:46,986
When Rasool Allah ﷺ made Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina

702
00:47:47,303 --> 00:47:51,574
he first settled with Bannu Amr Bin Auf(بنو عمرو بن عوف) who are on the outskirts of Madina

703
00:47:51,695 --> 00:47:54,159
 and this is where he built the Masjid(مسجد) of Quba'a(قباء).

704
00:47:54,281 --> 00:47:56,616
But he went to Madina, where did he stay.?

705
00:47:56,767 --> 00:47:58,459
He stayed with Bannu Najjar(بنونجَّار)

706
00:47:58,643 --> 00:48:03,182
and the men of Bannu Najjar(بنونجَّار) were surrounding Rasool Allah ﷺ carrying their swords.

707
00:48:03,691 --> 00:48:07,204
They were the private soldiers of Rasool Allah ﷺ

708
00:48:07,229 --> 00:48:12,780
and now he came to them to take the Bay'ah(بيعة) in their own camp.

709
00:48:12,873 --> 00:48:18,932
Umm-e-Ammarah(امّ عَمَّارَةْ) said: My husband held out his sword in his hand, because now this is Bay'ah(بيعة) to die.

710
00:48:18,972 --> 00:48:23,262
So, Umm-e-Ammarah(امّ عَمَّارَةْ) said: I pulled a pole that was holding the tent.

711
00:48:23,305 --> 00:48:28,726
I pulled it out and I held it in one hand and then I stuck a dagger in my waist belt

712
00:48:28,852 --> 00:48:31,622
and I was ready to fight, if anybody would come to me

713
00:48:31,671 --> 00:48:34,702
I will stab him, with the dagger and beat him, with the pole.

714
00:48:34,995 --> 00:48:38,781
This was the preparation of Umm-e-Ammarah رضي الله عنها.

715
00:48:38,948 --> 00:48:41,958
Even though, they were just taking the Bay'ah(بيعة) at that moment

716
00:48:41,983 --> 00:48:46,422
But she wanted to be ready to fight and defend Rasool Allah ﷺ.

717
00:48:46,518 --> 00:48:50,700
This is how, even the women of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم were

718
00:48:50,748 --> 00:48:56,037
and because she saw herself as belonging to Bannu Najjar(بنونجَّار), the fighters of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

719
00:48:56,140 --> 00:49:00,305
She has to take part in that and she has to be part of this fighting force.

720
00:49:00,368 --> 00:49:04,960
So, she prepared herself to fight and die for Rasool Allah ﷺ,

721
00:49:05,046 --> 00:49:09,850
a position that many men, strong men today are refusing to take.

722
00:49:09,940 --> 00:49:13,658
And then the other thing regarding the Bay'ah(بيعة) of Ar-Ridhwaan(ألرضوان),

723
00:49:13,746 --> 00:49:16,826
is the Bay'ah(بيعة) of Salamah Ibn Aqwa رضي الله عنه.

724
00:49:16,866 --> 00:49:19,887
We've been talking about Salamah(سلمة) a lot lately.

725
00:49:20,068 --> 00:49:24,534
Salamah(سلمة), Rasool Allah ﷺ called him to come and give Bay'ah(بيعة), so he gave Bay'ah(بيعة).

726
00:49:25,062 --> 00:49:30,378
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ saw that he doesn't have any protection, any armor, so he gave him Darqah(درقاه) or Juhfa(جهفه)

727
00:49:30,883 --> 00:49:34,401
and this is a very small shield, it's like size of a Frisbee

728
00:49:34,819 --> 00:49:38,239
and he gave it to him and then Salamah(سلمة) left.

729
00:49:38,617 --> 00:49:42,956
And he met with his uncle and his uncle didn't have any armor.

730
00:49:42,996 --> 00:49:44,480
 So, he gave him this shield.

731
00:49:44,834 --> 00:49:48,910
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ saw Salamah(سلمة) and told him come and give Bay'ah(بيعة).

732
00:49:49,078 --> 00:49:51,472
Salamah(سلمة) said: I have already given my Bay'ah(بيعة).

733
00:49:51,512 --> 00:49:53,249
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Give it again.

734
00:49:53,403 --> 00:49:55,359
So, Salamah(سلمة) gave his Bay'ah(بيعة) second time

735
00:49:55,399 --> 00:49:59,039
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: Where is the shield that I gave you?

736
00:49:59,190 --> 00:50:00,709
He said: I gave it to my Uncle.

737
00:50:01,445 --> 00:50:02,636
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

738
00:50:03,002 --> 00:50:07,764
مَثَلُكَ كَمَثَلِ الْقَائِلْ اَبْغِنِيْ حَبِيْبًا هُوَ اَحَبَّ اِلَيَّ مِنْ نَّفْسِيْ

739
00:50:07,898 --> 00:50:10,051
The example of you is like the one who said;

740
00:50:10,076 --> 00:50:13,291
O Allah give me somebody, whom I love more than myself.

741
00:50:14,206 --> 00:50:18,314
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ saw Salamah(سلمه) a third time and told him; Come and give me Bay'ah(بيعة)

742
00:50:18,537 --> 00:50:20,753
He said: O Rasool Ullah I have already done so.

743
00:50:20,793 --> 00:50:22,014
He said: Give it again.

744
00:50:22,199 --> 00:50:24,703
So, Salamah(سلمه) has given his Bay'ah(بيعة) three times.

745
00:50:24,907 --> 00:50:28,414
He has put his hand, in the hand of Rasool Allah ﷺ for three times

746
00:50:28,685 --> 00:50:30,434
to pledge that you would die for him.

747
00:50:30,554 --> 00:50:34,974
And the third thing to mention regarding Bay'at-Ur-Ridhwan(بيعت الرضوان),

748
00:50:35,565 --> 00:50:42,973
Ar-Rawafidh(الروافض), the Shia(شيعة), they say that Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) has not attended the Battle of Badr(بدر)

749
00:50:43,084 --> 00:50:45,790
and he has not given Bay'ah(بيعة) of Ar-Ridhwan(الرضوان).

750
00:50:46,408 --> 00:50:51,169
Now, we have already, I think talked about, why he didn't attend the Battle of Badr(بدر).

751
00:50:51,212 --> 00:50:56,172
It is because Rasool Allah ﷺ told him not to attend it and to stay behind with his wife

752
00:50:56,324 --> 00:50:59,376
the daughter of Rasool Allah ﷺ, who was on her deathbed.

753
00:50:59,620 --> 00:51:02,409
So, now why did the Uthman(عثمان) not give Bay'ah(بيعة)

754
00:51:02,969 --> 00:51:08,833
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), this is such a foolish thing to say about Uthman(عثمان).

755
00:51:08,983 --> 00:51:12,731
I mean, the whole Bay'ah(بيعة) was for the sake of Uthman(عثمان).

756
00:51:13,501 --> 00:51:14,107
That's one thing.

757
00:51:14,147 --> 00:51:17,350
The second thing is that he did give his Bay'ah(بيعة).

758
00:51:17,792 --> 00:51:22,092
Rasool Allah ﷺ put one of his hands in the other hand

759
00:51:22,155 --> 00:51:25,173
and said: This is the Bay'ah(بيعة) for Uthman(عثمان).

760
00:51:25,361 --> 00:51:30,258
So, Uthman(عثمان) didn't give the Bay'ah(بيعة), with his own hand, but it was even better.

761
00:51:30,337 --> 00:51:33,858
Rasool Allah ﷺ, gave the Bay'ah(بيعة) for him, with his own hand.

762
00:51:33,883 --> 00:51:37,365
The blessed hand of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

763
00:51:38,024 --> 00:51:39,465
Allahعزوجل says:

764
00:51:39,879 --> 00:51:48,621
اِنَّ أَرْسَلْنَاكَ شَاهِدًا وَمُبَشِّرًا وَنَذِيرًاَ۝

765
00:51:48,906 --> 00:51:51,731
We have truly sent thee, as a witness

766
00:51:52,024 --> 00:51:56,188
as a bringer of glad tidings, as a Warner.

767
00:51:56,904 --> 00:52:05,690
لِتُؤْمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ وَتُعَزِّرُوهُ وَتُوَقِّرُوهُ وَتُسَبِّحُوهُ

768
00:52:05,825 --> 00:52:11,039
وَتُسَبِّحُوهُ بُكْرَةً وَأَصِيلًاَ۝

769
00:52:11,546 --> 00:52:16,448
In order that you, O men may believe in Allah and His messenger

770
00:52:16,718 --> 00:52:22,399
that you may assist and honor Him and celebrate His praises morning and evening.

771
00:52:23,185 --> 00:52:33,377
الَّذِينَ يُبَايِعُونَكَ إِنَّمَا يُبَايِعُونَ اللَّهَ يَدُ اللَّهِ فَوْقَ أَيْدِيهِمْ ۚ

772
00:52:33,709 --> 00:52:39,437
 فَمَنْ نَكَثَ فَإِنَّمَا يَنْكُثُ عَلَىٰ نَفْسِهِ

773
00:52:39,714 --> 00:52:47,883
وَمَنْ أَوْفَىٰ بِمَا عَاهَدَ عَلَيْهُ اللَّهَ فَسَيُؤْتِيهِ أَجْرًا عَظِيمًا۝

774
00:52:48,293 --> 00:52:52,302
Verily, those who plight their fealty to thee

775
00:52:52,545 --> 00:52:56,065
do no less than plight their fealty to Allah

776
00:52:56,176 --> 00:52:58,827
the hand of Allah is over their hands

777
00:52:59,106 --> 00:53:05,101
then anyone who violates his oath, does so to the harm of his own soul.

778
00:53:05,288 --> 00:53:10,184
And anyone who fulfills what he has covenanted with Allah

779
00:53:10,267 --> 00:53:12,836
Allah will soon grant him a great reward.

780
00:53:12,887 --> 00:53:17,000
These Ayaat(آيات) were revealed that we talk about the Bay'ah(بيعة) of Ar-Ridhwan(ألرضوان).

781
00:53:17,560 --> 00:53:25,283
لَقَدْ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ إِذْ يُبَايِعُونَكَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ

782
00:53:26,287 --> 00:53:29,990
Allahسبحانه وتعالى says that the Allah is pleased with the believers

783
00:53:30,015 --> 00:53:32,337
إِذْ يُبَايِعُونَكَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ

784
00:53:32,498 --> 00:53:35,869
The ones, who have pledged their allegiance to you under the tree.

785
00:53:37,412 --> 00:53:39,025
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) says about this Ayah(آية).

786
00:53:39,065 --> 00:53:41,928
وَتُعَزِّرُوهُ اَنْ تُقَاتِلُوْبَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ بِسَّيْفْ

787
00:53:42,243 --> 00:53:46,246
Wa-Tuaziroohoo(وَتُعَزِّرُوهُ ), when the Ayah(آية) says, you give support to Rasool Allah ﷺ

788
00:53:46,292 --> 00:53:50,481
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) and Ikrimah(عكرمه) said: That you fight ahead of him with your swords

789
00:53:50,522 --> 00:53:52,897
you fight in front of him, with your swords.

790
00:53:52,922 --> 00:53:59,077
That is how the loyalty and the love of Rasool Allah ﷺ is practiced.

791
00:53:59,559 --> 00:54:01,053
This is the Bay'ah(بيعة) of Ar-Ridhwan(الرضوان)

792
00:54:01,113 --> 00:54:05,211
لَقَدْ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ إِذْ يُبَايِعُونَكَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ

793
00:54:05,480 --> 00:54:10,653
Allah is pleased with the believers, who pledged their allegiance to you, under the tree.

794
00:54:10,828 --> 00:54:11,788
This Bay'ah(بيعة),

795
00:54:12,082 --> 00:54:17,042
later on, it was discovered that Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) was not killed and it was a false rumor.

796
00:54:17,603 --> 00:54:22,358
But this was only a reason for this amazing event

797
00:54:22,737 --> 00:54:29,054
of pledging to die for the sake of Rasool Allah ﷺ, for the sake of protecting Islam.

798
00:54:29,676 --> 00:54:35,371
This event must have caused great terror in the hearts of the people of Quraish(قريش)

799
00:54:35,898 --> 00:54:41,792
to hear or to see that the Muslims have pledged to die, to the last man,

800
00:54:42,047 --> 00:54:46,765
to fight to the last man, for the sake of defending their religion.

801
00:54:47,012 --> 00:54:49,818
And this was an event witness by the heavens

802
00:54:50,509 --> 00:54:54,524
and the Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed the Ayaat(آيات) talking about this

803
00:54:55,083 --> 00:54:59,186
and when the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم finished, their Bay'ah(بيعة),

804
00:54:59,324 --> 00:55:01,114
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them.

805
00:55:01,273 --> 00:55:03,565
اَنْتُمْ خِيَّارُ اَهْلِ اَرْضْ

806
00:55:03,751 --> 00:55:06,425
You are the best people, on the face of the earth.

807
00:55:07,129 --> 00:55:10,074
And in another Hadith(حديث) it says,

808
00:55:10,154 --> 00:55:15,623
all of the people who have pledged their allegiance to Rasool Allah ﷺ are forgiven

809
00:55:15,831 --> 00:55:17,458
their sins are forgiven, for them.

810
00:55:17,697 --> 00:55:20,247
 اِلَّا صَاحِبُ الْجَمَلْ اَلاحْمَرْ

811
00:55:20,487 --> 00:55:23,666
Except for the owner of the red camel

812
00:55:24,022 --> 00:55:29,759
and this was Al-Jadd Bin Qais(ألجد بن قيس) who did not pledge, his allegiance to Rasool Allah ﷺ

813
00:55:29,903 --> 00:55:35,267
and one of the companion said: I saw him glued to the side of his camel

814
00:55:35,448 --> 00:55:39,113
hiding away from Rasool Allah ﷺ, so that he would not giving him Bay'ah(بيعة).

815
00:55:39,980 --> 00:55:44,599
And when we say that the classes of the different levels and the classes of Sahabah(صحابه).

816
00:55:44,632 --> 00:55:49,769
We say that they the best are the 10 who are given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة)

817
00:55:49,936 --> 00:55:52,247
and then following them are the people of Al-Badr(البدر)

818
00:55:52,377 --> 00:55:55,190
and then following them or the people of Bay'at-Ur-Ridhwan(بيعت الرضوان).

819
00:55:55,431 --> 00:55:58,247
These are the best of humanity.

820
00:55:59,134 --> 00:56:03,357
This is the Bay'ah(بيعة) of Ar-Ridhwan( الرضوان).

821
00:56:03,737 --> 00:56:07,048
Where the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم came to Rasool Allah ﷺ

822
00:56:07,112 --> 00:56:15,033
and offered to give up their lives for the sake of defending, the religion of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

823
00:56:15,058 --> 00:56:18,444
Now, we go back to the reason, the reason was Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان).

824
00:56:18,815 --> 00:56:25,488
So, this shows you that the Muslims were willing to fight and die for the sake of one man.

825
00:56:26,008 --> 00:56:30,961
One of their men and this shows us how the Ummah(امة).

826
00:56:31,778 --> 00:56:33,188
كَالْبُنْيَانَ الْمَرْصُوْصْ

827
00:56:33,682 --> 00:56:36,393
This is how the Ummah(امة) should be, like one body

828
00:56:37,068 --> 00:56:45,148
when part of the body feels the pain, than the entire body feels that pain and feels the fever.

829
00:56:45,407 --> 00:56:52,683
So, the entire Muslim force a 1400 men, stood up together for the sake of one man

830
00:56:52,882 --> 00:56:56,730
and that's Uthman Ibn Affan رضي الله عنه.

831
00:56:56,991 --> 00:57:03,272
In-Sha-Allah-Ho-Ta'ala(اِنْشاءالله تعالى), we'll carry on with the rest of the story of Al-Hudaybiyya(الحديبية),

832
00:57:03,557 --> 00:57:05,964
in our following session.

833
00:57:06,152 --> 00:57:12,112
وَصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

834
00:57:12,319 --> 00:57:14,797
واَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمةُ الله وَبَرَكَاتُه

